{"strongs": "H0399", "word": "קְרַץ", "translit": "a.khal", "root": "אול", "morph": "A:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "eat, devour", "definition": "[ אֲכַל ] verb eat, devour (Biblical Hebrew); — Pe`al Perfect 3 masculine plural אֲכַ֫לוּ Dan 3:8 ; Dan 6:25 Imperfect 3 masculine singular יֵאכֻל Dan 4:30 3 feminine singular תֵּאכֻל Dan 7:23 Imperative feminine singular אֲכֻּ֫לִי v Dan 7:5 Participle feminine singular אָֽכְלָה , v Dan 7:7 v Dan 7:9 — 1. eat , of beast, Dan 4:30 (accusative of thing). 2. devour , of beast in vision, Dan 7:5 (accusative of thing), absolute v Dan 7:7 v Dan 7:19 hence figurative of kingdom, devour, devastate , v Dan 7:23 (accusative of earth). 3. in phrase ק־רְצֵיהוֺן ׳ א Dan 3:8 eat their pieces , i.e. slander them, compare Dan 6:25 (see קְרַץ ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9297')\">BDB9297</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H398')\">H398</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H399')\">H399</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9296')\">BDB9296</entry> | BIBLICAL ARAMAIC | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9298')\">BDB9298</entry></div><p> [<bdbarc>אֲכַל</bdbarc>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>eat, devour</highlightword> (Biblical Hebrew); — <div class=\"point\"><b>Pe`al</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 3 masculine plural <bdbarc>אֲכַ֫לוּ</bdbarc> <ref ref=\"Dan 3:8\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(27,3,8)\">Dan 3:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Dan 6:25\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(27,6,25)\">Dan 6:25</ref> <highlight>Imperfect</highlight> 3 masculine singular <bdbarc>יֵאכֻל</bdbarc> <ref ref=\"Dan 4:30\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(27,4,30)\">Dan 4:30</ref> 3 feminine singular<bdbarc>תֵּאכֻל</bdbarc> <ref ref=\"Dan 7:23\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(27,7,23)\">Dan 7:23</ref> <highlight>Imperative</highlight> feminine singular <bdbarc>אֲכֻּ֫לִי</bdba